WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.480
So do guys...

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.960
prefer girls like Sakurazaka-san 
who are earnest and family-oriented?

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.130
Huh? Where's this coming from?

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.490
What do they like girls to do for them?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.740
There's no point in asking me, is there?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.000
Really? But you said you'd help me, didn't you?

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.860
If you don't give me answers, 
you get nothing but rice.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.080
What?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.000
Think about it seriously.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.680
All right. Things guys like 
having done for them, huh?

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.100
Hmm...

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.010
Making them lunch, maybe?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.810
Lunch?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.880
Yup. A home-cooked boxed 
lunch filled with love.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.140
Really?

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.180
Especially from you, 
since no one would expect it.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.160
No one would expect it, you say?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.320
S-Sorry!

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.900
But that might work! 
And you're gonna help me, right?

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.300
I am?

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:04.740
<i>What percentage does "like" have 
to hit before you can call it "love"?</i>

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.850
<i>It's criminal to be so shy</i>

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.710
<i>Intelligence and wild fancies, 
tick tock, just pick a mood</i>

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.000
<i>A drizzle from a patch of blue sky</i>

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.300
<i>No less than supreme</i>

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.710
<i>A maiden's heart zigzags, 
cute and invincible</i>

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.320
<i>The wild ringing of bells</i>

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:38.430
<i>What percentage does "like" have 
to hit before you can call it "love"?</i>

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.110
<i>Hold me so tightly that I fall asleep</i>

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.660
<i>A daydream that seems like fiction</i>

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.700
<i>Give me a kiss that breaks 
the expectant silence of the play</i>

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.120
<i>Give that indecision a tight embrace, too</i>

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.740
<i>My heart hurts and hurts,</i>

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:00.630
<i>racing unpredictably 
with joy and excitement</i>

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.110
<i>It's TRUE FOOL LOVE! Hold me tight!</i>

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.430
<i>Be brave, my darling</i>

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:09.010
<i>It won't all be happy and fun</i>

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.030
<i>It's all up to us</i>

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.220
<i>ONCE MORE SMILE, TWICE MORE CHIME</i>

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.890
<i>Please look my way, darling</i>

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:25.990
<i>Please notice my pure love for you</i>

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:34.100
<i>And so I began helping Watanabe 
with her boxed lunch strategy.</i>

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.430
This is a pretty extravagant dinner!

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.950
I want to choose the lineup

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.150
for the boxed lunch from among these, 
keeping the color variety in mind.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.330
How is it?

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.840
It's great!

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.560
But I think I prefer my rolled omelets sweet.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.880
Huh? I'm not asking about 
your preferences here.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.870
Minami-kun has a mature vibe to him,

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.550
so rolled omelets with 
sugar in them won't work.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.050
Then don't ask me.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.920
I'm really proud of the mini hamburger 
patties and this ohitashi salad.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.050
Yeah?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.680
And I think I might need a 
rolled omelet pan after all...

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.940
Whoa, what's that? It's not a home-cooked 
lunch from Akari-chan, is it?!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.340
Well, yeah.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.810
Seriously, Jiro-chan, you're way too blessed.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.070
It makes me want to ask, 
"O gods, have I done something wrong?"

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.360
But you guys are doing fine, too.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.590
No way. There's no love there at all.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:48.580
But in the beginning, I'd get 
nervous just eating together.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.910
<i>Morning! I've been waiting for you!</i>

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:56.090
Hashimoto Marin
"Morning! I've been waiting for you."

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.770
It's already afternoon, though.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.090
Right now, both "good morning" and 
"goodnight" are just game functions.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.130
Like collecting login bonuses.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.090
Just be glad you even get bonuses.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.070
What?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.230
I don't want to hear that from 
a guy whose relationship chart

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.050
looks like it's from an erotic manga.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:14.840
Hurry up and let that gyaru wife you live 
with wreck that factory-fresh unit of yours.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.860
Quit saying such disturbing things!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.790
And there it is!

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.720
He's calling the lucky event of graduating 
from virgin status "disturbing"!

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.800
Are you one of those harem manga leads who,

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.950
for some reason, don't yield 
even when cornered by beauties?

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.120
So, um, how is it really?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.080
D-Does stuff like that happen?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:32.780
Does it?

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.960
No, it doesn't!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:40.840
<b>Potato Star</b>

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:40.840
<b>Lightly Salted</b>

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:40.840
<b>So delicious you won't 
be able to stop!</b>

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:37.600
<i>She only ever wears skimpy, flimsy clothes.</i>

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.140
<i>I think I deserve praise for the 
self-restraint it takes to live with her!</i>

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.650
Jiro!

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.850
Let's stop talking about this already.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.980
We're eating,

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.490
and besides, it'll make things awkward 
with Watanabe when I get home.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.890
What about me?

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.020
What about Watanabe?

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.440
Uh-oh. How much did you hear?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.530
G-Greetings. How are you this afternoon?

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.690
Huh?

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.880
Uh, nothing. Sorry.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.200
So it was something you 
feel the need to apologize for?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.550
No, um... W-We were talking 
about Tanabe-kun, and, um...

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.790
So how was the lunch I made?

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.040
I-It was really good.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.770
Huh? That's it?

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:23.640
Um, the bacon-wrapped 
asparagus was awesome.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.510
Good, good. What else?

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.800
Well...

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:30.120
I really do think I prefer 
my rolled omelets sweet.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.300
I told you, I don't need 
to know <i>your</i> preferences.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.810
What? Then don't ask me.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.790
There's other stuff you could tell me!

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:41.160
Like how it all looked together, or if it 
was okay after being in the box so long,

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.530
or what you thought of the taste!

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.720
I told you what I thought of the taste!

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:48.420
I need answers that are more useful 
as reference, or there's no point!

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:49.880
And now, a tanka...

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.560
Standing before me

00:05:50.870 --> 00:06:00.170
<b>Standing before me
They force me to watch as they
Have their lovers' spat</b>

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.920
They force me to watch as they

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.530
Have their lovers' spat

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:00.170
<b>I am not envious, no
Instead, I shall remember
Kamo</b>

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:56.930
I am not envious, no

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.120
Instead, I shall remember

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.170
Kamo

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.670
<b>Lancia</b>

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.670
m 0 0 l 185 0 l 185 50 l 0 50

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.670
<b>What do we need to do
to defeat that guy?</b>

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.670
m 0 0 l 350 0 l 350 60 l 0 60

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.670
<b>Don't worry. I'm sure we'll win.
Let's find our opponent's weakness.</b>

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.160
Morning.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.190
Wow, that's amazing!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.690
Right? It's a boxed lunch for Minami-kun!

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.040
I thought I'd take it to the place 
where he works part-time.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.960
Oh, so it's the real test 
at last, huh? Sounds good.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.260
S-Sorry. It just looks so 
good, I couldn't help it.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.960
I'm really proud of today's rolled omelets.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.710
Are you sure? It's for Tenjin, isn't it?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.360
It's the end piece. It'll just 
end up leftover, anyway.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:54.300
<i>Nope, still not sweet.</i>

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.810
<i>The lunch that my mock wife 
makes belong to Tenjin.</i>

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.810
<i>But Tenjin's wife, Shiori, 
is the one I have feelings for.</i>

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.320
<i>There really isn't any sweetness here.</i>

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.450
Okay!

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.920
Isn't it a little too showy?

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.950
It's better than looking boring, isn't it?

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:20.960
<i>How many hours did she spend 
dressing up to deliver one lunch?</i>

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.230
<i>She'll be meeting a guy, right?</i>

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.680
<i>Lots of things are showing.</i>

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:26.230
<i>She seems a little... obvious.</i>

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:29.240
<i>When she's out with me, 
she just wears whatever.</i>

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.220
<i>She's never worn anything like that.</i>

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:32.950
Yakuin?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.440
U-Um... I'm gonna do my very best, okay?

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.480
So...

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.380
Yakuin...

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.860
Do the goodbye thing.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.490
Huh?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.580
Like you did that other time.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:58.580
<i>The "goodbye thing"? She can't mean...</i>

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.890
Please, Yakuin?

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.640
No, I-I can't! My heart isn't ready!

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.680
What? You're saying this <i>now</i>?

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.850
You said you'd cheer me on, didn't you?

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.970
But you're going out to see Tenjin, right?

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.010
Are you sure you want that... from me?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.050
Moron.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.410
It's yours I want, Yakuin.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.060
It made me feel really safe that other time.

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:20.300
Huh?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.920
<i>If you say something like that 
with that look on your face...</i>

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.120
<i>Any guy would get his hopes up!</i>

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.450
I-I'll get it.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.020
Yes?

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.200
<i>Shiori?</i>

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.560
Sorry for showing up unannounced.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.960
I'm so glad the two of you are home!

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.600
Nah, I've never got anything to do.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.590
He doesn't have many friends, after all.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.760
Oh, I brought apple pies. 
I kind of made too many.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.590
Really?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.140
You made these?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.230
Wow! They look delicious!

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.480
Thanks. It was a request from Minami-kun.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.280
Minami-kun seems to like sweet things, 
so I made them to suit his tastes.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.960
I hope both of you like them, too.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:16.990
Really?

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.990
Who would've thought, huh?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.740
Oh! How cute!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.750
A boxed lunch? Are you going 
on a picnic or something?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:29.000
No, that's... well, uh...

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.910
It's really amazing...

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.880
They look delicious.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.540
<i>Taking a home-cooked lunch on a picnic?</i>

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.640
<i>That seems lovely.</i>

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.140
Man, that was good.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.740
Thanks for such a feast.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.530
Come on, cheer up!

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.160
Next time, you can go for a time 
when Tenjin's by himself. Right?

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:10.730
Minami-kun likes sweet things.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.960
That's right! You can research 
his favorite foods and—

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.420
What else do I have?

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:17.270
Huh?

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:23.100
After what you said, I thought 
I could get by on my cooking.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.960
<i>Watanabe is always so confident.</i>

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.510
<i>This is the first time I've 
seen her so discouraged.</i>

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:30.890
<i>She worked so hard.</i>

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.790
<i>There's nothing to do about it now, 
but it's throwing me off a bit.</i>

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.380
Watanabe, you've got tons more good points!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.370
You're cheerful and articulate.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.410
You can make friends with anyone.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.340
And the guys all talk about you a lot.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.950
They think you're great.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.880
Great how?

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:47.800
Huh?

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.910
What's great about me?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.930
Um, well, you know...

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.920
You're... I guess "sexy" is the word, 
and you're b-beautiful...

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:58.060
Y-You have a great figure, and you 
make daring fashion choices, so...

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.140
So?

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:03.390
You know, like... you're every guy's dream, 
the object of their desires...

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.980
I mean... How do I put it?

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.440
Basically, any guy would 
want to have se—er, uh...

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.200
Wait! That's not what I meant! 
It's really not!

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.690
It's just, all guys think about 
stuff like that, so, um...

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.960
It's more... as a woman, 
you're very appealing?

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.540
You know, like, they have those 
celebrity rankings of, um...

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.010
I mean, uh...

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:25.080
You, too?

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.330
Huh? M-Me?

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:31.420
<i>Me and Watanabe...</i>

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.440
Um, well...

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:34.400
Zing

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:34.860
Zing

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.340
I-I've never really thought about it.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.090
Liar.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.220
Huh? Um...

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:58.500
Have you thought of doing 
things like this with me?

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.790
Have you, Yakuin?

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.460
You've thought about doing things 
like this with me, haven't you?

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.580
How many times?

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.960
When do you think about it?

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.970
Watanabe...

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.880
Time out! Hang on!

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.470
Why? You wanted to try it sometime, didn't you?

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:31.980
Go ahead.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.170
I'll grant your wish.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.480
<i>It was for real.</i>

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.410
<i>Gyaru really are like 
they are in erotic manga.</i>

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.370
<i>Is it really okay for me 
to graduate this easily?</i>

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.870
<i>Wait... I have this incredibly uneasy feeling.</i>

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:57.880
Yakuin...

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:04.880
We can't!

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.010
We can't.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.970
Th-This is...

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.180
s-something you do with 
someone you love, right?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.360
<i>Oh, man. It's over.</i>

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.860
<i>Why did I stop her?</i>

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.180
<i>It was my chance to graduate!</i>

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.290
You didn't want to.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.120
I mean, for one thing, you have Tenjin.

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.860
And you have Sakurazaka-san.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:36.290
I see.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.030
Watanabe?

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.590
Let's stop this married couple thing.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.260
<i>And so our married life broke apart.</i>

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.270
<i>Why did things turn out this way?</i>

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:08.230
We could've just muddled through 
this marriage practical thing...

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.680
But now, because I overstepped 
my bounds and got presumptuous...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>9th</b>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>8th</b>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>Najima Nakano</b>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>Miyajidake Asahi</b>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>Sakurazaka Shiori</b>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>Tenjin Minami</b>

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.480
Minami-kun, you're amazing!

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.210
You can cook, too?

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.020
I rotate with Shiori.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.940
Shiori, what's wrong?

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:43.940
It's nothing.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>74th</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>Okubo Osamu</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>Shuto Kyoko</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>75th</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>Yakuin Jiro</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>Watanabe Akari</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.440
<b>Omure Yutaka</b>

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.950
Jiro-chan!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.520
Whoa, man! Think about time, 
place, and occasion, would you?

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.230
What's the meaning of that?

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.270
Of what?

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.130
The month-end evaluation!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:03.430
Hey, Jiro-chan, what happened?

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:06.150
If there was a reason for it, 
it was your fault, right?

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:08.660
What's it matter? Just leave it alone.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.390
I wonder what the right choice would've been.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.100
<i>At first, I thought she 
was just making fun of me.</i>

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:25.690
<i>I thought that after she made me take her 
seriously, she'd laugh and call me stupid.</i>

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.570
<i>But her hand...</i>

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.500
<i>was shockingly cold and trembling.</i>

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.870
<i>Her nervousness and uncertainty 
became painfully clear to me.</i>

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.050
<i>She's probably the same as me.</i>

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.880
<i>It seemed like it was all new to her, too...</i>

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:46.370
<i>Any guy would want to have se—</i>

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.380
It's cold.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:53.270
<i>If that's true, then...</i>

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.890
I'm the absolute worst.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.390
What's this all of a sudden?

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:03.260
Jiro-chan, don't you have a handkerchief?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.620
Oh, Shiori.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.150
Hey, Jiro-kun...

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.150
Do you have a little time to 
talk with me, just the two of us?

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.360
Sure.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.780
Are you serious?

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.410
Wow!

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:20.410
The breeze feels so nice.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.920
Shiori, is what you wanted to talk about...

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:27.670
Jiro-kun, did something happen 
between you and Watanabe-san?

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.860
Yeah. You could call it a fight,

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.210
or you could say I didn't 
express myself well...

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.800
I had the wrong idea about her.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.960
But I couldn't find the 
right timing to apologize.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:43.980
And Watanabe doesn't seem 
like she wants to talk to me.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.300
Even though you're living together?

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:47.020
Huh?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:51.570
In a day's time, you're with her 
more than you're with anyone else.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:55.210
I think Watanabe-san will understand you.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:59.580
I've been your friend since we were 
little, so I can vouch for you!

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:01.880
That makes us even, right?

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.180
Shiori...

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.290
I really don't stand a chance against you.

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:10.090
You've always beaten me 
when it comes to discussions.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:14.030
I'm very much still your 
childhood friend, after all.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.250
Ahem!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.270
Still, I was impressed you'd noticed
that something was wrong.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:23.600
Though, I guess anyone who saw that 
month-end evaluation would know.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.040
It makes me feel jealous.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:37.110
I'm back.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.120
600 watts
2 min. 30 sec.

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:57.380
Watanabe, I'd like to talk for a minute...

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.140
But, yeah, you're not gonna come out, huh?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.980
So come in, then.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.000
<i>It smells like a girl!</i>

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.150
<i>I didn't expect her to 
just ignore my existence.</i>

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.160
S-So, um, I'm sorry about before.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.830
It's not like you did anything wrong.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:27.660
No!

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:29.760
It's all my fault!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.950
That was just me trying too 
hard and getting nowhere!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:34.820
Don't make me say it all out loud!

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.420
It's fine, so just forget all of it!

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.430
Right now!

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.930
Look, it seems like you got 
the wrong idea, so I'll say this...

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:50.630
It's not like I didn't want to, okay?

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:52.440
I am a guy, after all.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.070
And to tell the truth, 
it's just like you said.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:58.190
I've had wild fantasies 
about you more than once.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:02.580
And, well, I'm actually really grateful 
to you for that experience...

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.120
That's enough!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.170
Are you stupid?!

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.680
Don't say all that! Are you stupid?!

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:08.200
It's sexual harassment!

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:11.470
You're in a girl's room, and you have zero tact!

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.660
And that's why you'll never 
be able to "graduate"!

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.710
Y-You're quite right.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:19.200
But the reason I stopped you then was...

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.430
I just... I don't really know, but...

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:26.220
I just felt like I had to treat 
you with more care than that.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:29.590
The idea of doing something like 
that in the heat of the moment

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:31.730
just made me feel uneasy somehow.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.980
I don't really get it, but...

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:36.600
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.730
It's the same now!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.700
I really hate things being 
this awkward between us.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:44.310
I want to be able to talk to you 
normally, like we did before.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.990
And I want to eat together.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.250
Would you please give me a chance?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:01.510
Watanabe, I want to be...

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.670
a married couple with you again.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:17.970
No! Not like that!

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:19.960
When I said "married couple," 
I meant the practical!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.600
O-O-Of course I realize that you have Tenjin!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.780
I'm not going to get in the way of that... er...

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:26.780
Pff...

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:27.660
Pff?

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:30.720
Oh, man!

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:33.300
What? Why are you laughing?

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:34.920
You're acting so desperate!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:39.070
And what was all that? 
A proposal? That's hilarious!

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:44.050
W-Well, you said we should 
stop being a married couple!

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:46.920
Huh? But we can't stop.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.060
It's something the school decided.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.300
What?!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:53.040
So that was a lie, then?!

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.360
You lied?!

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.560
Why?!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:59.070
How scary. It wasn't a lie. More of a vibe.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:02.460
Do you have any idea how 
much I agonized over this?

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:08.220
I think I'm enjoying this married 
life more than I thought I would.

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:15.330
I like you quite a lot, Jiro.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.960
<i>What is this?</i>

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.760
<i>Why'd she suddenly use my first name?</i>

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:23.060
<i>What does she mean by "like"?</i>

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.120
What about you, Jiro?

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:29.100
<i>I...</i>

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:37.230
A hand?

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:41.480
Just kidding! Too bad for you!

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:45.490
Sometimes the heat of the moment 
is important, Repressed-kun.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.990
Watanabe...

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:50.640
Welcome home, Jiro.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.050
Good to be back.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.200
<i>We're not going back to square one.</i>

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:58.850
<i>We're starting from zero.</i>

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:14.060
<i>I like you quite a lot, Jiro.</i>

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:18.140
I said it.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:23.920
<i>In this moment when I've 
deceived you on a cosmic scale</i>

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:28.350
<i>I want to give love a try</i>

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:31.260
<i>In this night when everything 
begins to overflow</i>

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:33.530
<i>I match my stride to yours</i>

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:39.370
<i>The clock hands stop, 
charmed by a fleeting curse</i>

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:43.940
<i>The answers always slip away</i>

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:47.360
<i>All I want is to do it over again</i>

00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:52.760
<i>If I did, would this unsettling 
gloom inside me disappear?</i>

00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:57.060
<i>I want to know where my heart is hiding</i>

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:01.840
<i>One day this will end</i>

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:04.640
<i>I know that</i>

00:23:04.640 --> 00:23:06.350
<i>And I know the signs of discord</i>

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:08.400
<i>Turn them inside out</i>

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:10.000
<i>Don't let them pile up</i>

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:14.210
<i>I don't want things to 
stay unfinished like this</i>

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:18.250
<i>In this moment when I've 
deceived you on a cosmic scale</i>

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:22.680
<i>I want to give love a try</i>

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:24.700
<i>Everything begins to overflow</i>

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:27.890
<i>On this day when we don't know 
how much time is left to us</i>

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:36.150
<i>I want your thoughts to drift 
toward me fondly, again and again</i>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:53.740
Burned

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:53.310
A burned rolled omelet.

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:55.490
Akari, fretting.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:58.120
And standing behind her...

00:23:58.120 --> 00:23:59.750
Jiro, holding sugar.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:00.770
So it's your fault?

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:02.250
<b>Ow, ow, ow</b>

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:02.250
<b>Ow, ow, ow</b>

00:24:00.770 --> 00:24:02.250
I thought it'd taste better that way!

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:03.500
<b>SHFF</b>

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.020
You'd better take responsibility for it.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:05.000
<b>GULP</b>

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:05.000
<b>GULP</b>

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.000
<b>CHOMP</b>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.500
<b>Ow!</b>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.500
<b>Ow!</b>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.500
<b>I'm sorry</b>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.500
It's bitter...

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:10.010
A Hero, but Not the Main Character.

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:07.690
Next time...

00:24:07.690 --> 00:24:09.790
"A Hero, but Not the Main Character."
